                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "106dec4c-41c3-3f19-8e74-6e984f0ec0ef",
                        "entry_id": "3c4ec833-a05d-3692-8694-4c77a89c9bd4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "хрупкое стекловидное аморфное вещество красноватого или жёлтоватого цвета, получаемое из смолы хвойных деревьев и используемое в технических целях"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0f433356-2a8b-4dd1-8458-c358b070fa27",
                                "sense_id": "106dec4c-41c3-3f19-8e74-6e984f0ec0ef",
                                "text": "Он потянулся к скрипке, поджидавшей хозяина в открытом футляре, и любовно натер канифолью смычок."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bbdd3c44-8e6e-459c-a252-a486b5b18ce2",
                                "sense_id": "106dec4c-41c3-3f19-8e74-6e984f0ec0ef",
                                "text": "Затем нагретый паяльник погружают в порошок нашатыря или канифоли; если при этом появился легкий дымок, значит, паяльник готов к работе."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "49ff5382-2013-4afb-9e8c-e38c32d119d6",
                        "source_entry_id": "3c4ec833-a05d-3692-8694-4c77a89c9bd4",
                        "source_sense_id": "106dec4c-41c3-3f19-8e74-6e984f0ec0ef",
                        "target_lang_word": "rosin",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "rosin",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a5bca422-1d75-362a-8960-e73a4bb3a758",
                                        "entry_id": "618eb879-9a02-3c4f-8cce-a1eb1694c04c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A solid form of resin, obtained from liquid resin by vaporizing its volatile components."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0a6727a5-c6a7-4d2e-b1da-2e7f02e61ce1",
                                                "sense_id": "a5bca422-1d75-362a-8960-e73a4bb3a758",
                                                "text": "The action of the bow therefore depends almost entirely upon the application of rosin and upon its frictional properties. Violin rosin is a natural gum obtained from conifers such as larch that produce turpentine."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a957e45a-01b9-310b-964a-3307193f6d23",
                                        "entry_id": "618eb879-9a02-3c4f-8cce-a1eb1694c04c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Resin."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8ebebf90-b0fc-4f89-b196-a434b8060b6b",
                                                "sense_id": "a957e45a-01b9-310b-964a-3307193f6d23",
                                                "text": "‘It is delicate,’ said Pansa, ‘but there is perhaps the least particle too much of rosin in its flavor.’"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e48df3a9-1364-48f4-8d61-500b54f2c7f2",
                                                "sense_id": "a957e45a-01b9-310b-964a-3307193f6d23",
                                                "text": "From three o'clock onward they would be burning rosin and pitch pine (the sign of preparation), and so one had the picturesque spectacle of a rank, some two or three miles long, of tall, ascending columns of coal-black smoke; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cbf7c9c3-cc83-4a9c-8b1e-bba530471abf",
                                                "sense_id": "a957e45a-01b9-310b-964a-3307193f6d23",
                                                "text": "A thick, fat smoke oozed out from the fire, and a heavy smell of burned rosin and singed hair filled the air."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "rosin",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9442b568-d0d4-360a-9b56-70fa074b91d1",
                                        "entry_id": "c2d2dce3-8bb6-344b-b410-7b516c19bea9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To apply rosin to (something); to rub or cover with rosin."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fbd60e17-d89b-4b08-8e5e-6c64654c5f0d",
                                                "sense_id": "9442b568-d0d4-360a-9b56-70fa074b91d1",
                                                "text": "We waited expectantly as the guest violinist rosined his bow in preparation for playing."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0240fd08-2940-447f-aeba-472406dd366c",
                                                "sense_id": "9442b568-d0d4-360a-9b56-70fa074b91d1",
                                                "text": "The devil opened up his case and he said, \"I'll start this show.\"\nAnd fire flew from his fingertips as he rosined up his bow."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a1958bc3-2061-4287-8705-813c03f11dd5",
                        "source_entry_id": "3c4ec833-a05d-3692-8694-4c77a89c9bd4",
                        "source_sense_id": "106dec4c-41c3-3f19-8e74-6e984f0ec0ef",
                        "target_lang_word": "colophony",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "colophony",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6078db68-9026-3ea4-8b9f-c313b2157f89",
                                        "entry_id": "adbee10d-cff3-3297-90f8-27442093e0dd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Rosin; the residue left after the distillation of oil of turpentine from liquid resin, used in pharmaceutical preparations, soldering fluxes, and by violinists."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "23000023-24ab-418e-be27-f6e7c37fbc52",
                                                "sense_id": "6078db68-9026-3ea4-8b9f-c313b2157f89",
                                                "text": "This resin or turpentine is a very interesting and peculiar substance, or rather series of substances. It is valuable because tar, pitch, rosin, and colophony are obtained by distilling it."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
